Miriam,<br />
<br />
Keystone closed Claim File 2024-PL-0771 on Friday: indemnity zero, defense =
costs $92,400, no premium impact. A $3,675,000 demand, withdrawn in full, r=
eserved nothing. That is the good news, and it is worth being precise about=
 why it nearly went the other way.<br />
<br />
Nobody did anything wrong in 2011 - the opposite. Arthur identified the cla=
im, put the limitations risk in writing, recommended preserving it, and obt=
ained a written, signed scope limitation when the client chose otherwise. T=
he failure was everything after. The 2016 Novarra migration dropped pre-201=
4 matter correspondence, and the Matter Scope field was populated from the =
engagement letter alone, so the one system everyone treats as the file said=
 our engagement was unlimited - and said it with confidence. By 2024, every=
 person who knew better was gone: Arthur retired, Tenniel gone from Torvane=
, Wisner in-house, Hagerman deceased. Torvane's side had lost the same corr=
espondence to its own platform changes and an acquisition. Two companies, t=
wo document systems, one answer between them, and the answer was wrong in b=
oth.<br />
<br />
The claim died for one reason: the mail journal archive - the system nobody=
 works in, that was never migrated because it is not a system of record - s=
till held the 2011 sequence and the 2013 audit correspondence, intact and h=
ash-verifiable, and Howell's team produced them in fourteen minutes of sear=
ch and a few days of review. Our defense was not in our file. It was in our=
 email.<br />
<br />
Recommendations for the executive committee, which I will bring formally in=
 April: first, a journal-archive search becomes a standard step in every cl=
aim intake and every pre-2016 file retrieval, not an act of desperation on =
day thirty-two; second, Records certifies annually that the archive's reten=
tion and hash-verification are intact; third, on any matter where the scope=
 changes after the engagement letter, the change is papered as a profiled s=
upplemental letter, not left in correspondence - Novarra's scope field shou=
ld never again be the only thing a claims lawyer can find.<br />
<br />
Evelyn